Article 5 (Statistical Surveys and Database on Fisheries and Fishing Villages)
(1) The fisheries database to be established pursuant to Article 32 (2) of the Act shall cover the following:
1. Matters concerning fisheries management, including operating conditions and fishing performance by business type and fishing area for coastal and offshore fisheries, aquaculture, and distant-water fisheries;
2. Distribution of fisheries resources, status of projects for creation and recovery of fisheries resources, evaluation results, etc.;
3. Status of fisheries management and fishers;
4. Matters concerning policies for the promotion and fostering of fisheries and fishing villages;
5. Matters related to analysis of the economic effects of fisheries and fishing-village policies;
6. Other matters deemed by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries necessary for statistical surveys and database establishment for the development of fisheries and fishing villages.
(2) Pursuant to Article 32 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall entrust the conduct of statistical surveys on fisheries and fishing villages and the establishment of the fisheries database to any of the following institutions or organizations:
1. Public institutions under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
2. Government-funded research institutes under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Research Institutes, etc.;
3. Schools under Article 2, subparagraphs 1 through 6 of the Higher Education Act that have research personnel and facilities related to fisheries;
4. Nonprofit corporations established under Article 32 of the Civil Act that conduct policy research or informatization affairs in the fisheries sector;
5. Other institutions or organizations recognized by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries as having professional personnel and organizations necessary to perform affairs relating to the promotion and development of fisheries.
